From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: USA-RedDragon <USA-RedDragon@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 18:46:39 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] fix(clarify): a background subagent can ask the user a
 question

clarify was blocked for every delegate_task child, so a question a subagent
had always went through its parent. A direct child of a chat that can show a
question now gets clarify. Its question is a normal clarify card of the
parent's chat, named 'Subagent "<goal>" asks: ...', with the subagent goal
on the pending prompt next to the question, on every surface that shows the
chat's own questions (web, Telegram). It waits the configured clarify
timeout and returns the answer, or the usual timed_out reply, to the child.

The question belongs to the chat, not to the turn that spawned the child:
the turn's end keeps it (and the asker that shows the next one) while the
chat has live subagents, the session authority lists and answers it from any
later turn or an idle chat (which reads as waiting), and a typed message
answers it only while it waits for free text, so a message meant for the
idle chat never cancels a choice card. A child that an orchestrator joins
inline, a session that joins its children, and a chat with no card surface
keep the old behavior: no clarify tool.
